questions.question:
An analyst at a fund of hedge funds reviews a fund’s legal documents before subscribing. She finds that:

- the offering memorandum (OM) offers quarterly liquidity with 90 days’ notice, while the website and pitch book describe monthly liquidity;
- the limited partnership agreement is dated as of March 2025 but contains a gate provision that the manager says was added in October 2025;
- the law firm named in the OM confirms that it drafted the original documents.

Which action is most appropriate?
